      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, there is a significant methodological flaw identified in your data regarding the treatment of the control group's variance with a non-standard, zero-skew assumption that is inappropriate for biological samples. This likely invalidates the reported p-value of 0.04 and is precisely the concern raised by Reviewer 3, making the results unreliable without correction. To salvage this potential \"paradigm shift\" for your special issue, you will need to re-run the analysis with the correct standard deviation estimation and address the statistical discrepancy directly in the manuscript.",
