      "content": "That is... problematic. If we pull this now, the entire \"Quantum breakthroughs\" issue is basically dead in the water. Our partners have already staked their marketing budgets on this release, and a retraction or a major correction this late would be a massive blow to the journal's reputation for rigor. \n\nIs it truly a \"preclude publication\" level issue? Or is there a way we could frame this as a minor technical nuance in the discussion section so we don't lose the momentum of the Zhang paper? Given the groundbreaking nature of the other findings in the paper, could we just treat the p-value as a rough guide rather than a definitive proof?",
